# Fixed defect 567, 2026-10-10 (found by lane b18-ffi beside its work).
# Symptom: `x: i8 @ -128`, `y: i8 @ -1`, `print(x / y)` printed -128 at exit 0,
# where spec § 7 aborts on overflow at every width, and clang warned on the
# guard at `-O2`. Cause: the guard of `/` and `%` compared with `INT64_MIN`
# at every width, a comparison an `int8_t` can never satisfy, so it never
# fired, and C computed in `int` and the store wrapped (at `i32` it is C's
# undefined quotient). Repair: the guard takes the operands' own width's
# smallest value (`emit/division.hero`), and an unsigned width none.
# This case: every quotient and remainder that fits, printed: the smallest of
# each signed width by 1 and by 2, one above it by -1, and each unsigned width,
# whose `/` and `%` overflow nothing and take no guard (`u8 x / 2` warned).

function main()
    a: i8 @ -128
    b: i8 @ -127
    print(a / 1, a / 2, b / -1, a % 1, b % -1)
    c: i16 @ -32768
    d: i16 @ -32767
    print(c / 1, c / 2, d / -1, c % 7, d % -1)
    e: i32 @ -2147483648
    f: i32 @ -2147483647
    print(e / 1, e / 2, f / -1, e % 9, f % -1)
    g: u8 @ 255
    h: u16 @ 65535
    i: u32 @ 4294967295
    j: u64 @ 18446744073709551615
    print(g / 2, g % 2, h / 3, h % 4, i / 5, i % 6, j / 7, j % 8)
